  "sequence": 209,
  "subject": {
    "id": "small-shop-compiler-reanchor-boundary",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Reanchor the compiler program on the controlled Small Shop consumer.",
  "why": "The revision-21 foundation fixes OKG-FX001 and the deterministic compiler boundary. This transaction preserves the three existing corpora as independent controls, pauses their oracle producers without rewriting owned semantics, activates only controlled Small Shop inputs, and leaves the independent Small Shop oracle and research-local source-to-ABox vertical unassigned."
